  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the most probable outcome of each lottery and prefers the one with the more favorable such outcome. In this case, Lottery A has a most probable outcome of 3000 Euros (90%), while Lottery B has a most probable outcome of 0 Euros (55%). The individual’s verbal report emphasizes the attractiveness of the 90% chance in A and the aversion to the less than 50% chance in B, which aligns with focusing on the high-probability outcomes. Although the individual does not explicitly state that they are comparing the most probable outcomes, their reasoning is consistent with attending to the outcome that comes with the highest probability in each lottery. They prefer A because of its high chance of winning, which corresponds to its most probable outcome being favorable. The justification, while not explicitly structured around the concept of 'most probable outcome,' reflects a decision rule that prioritizes the lottery with the high-probability winning outcome over one with a lower probability of winning, even if the potential prize is larger. This closely matches the logic of the decision reason. Therefore, the information considered (high probability of winning in A, low in B) and the justification (preference due to high chance of winning) align well with the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

